1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,816
Why do smart people stay in

2
00:00:01,816 --> 00:00:02,959
draining careers,

3
00:00:02,959 --> 00:00:04,506
dead-end side projects,

4
00:00:04,506 --> 00:00:07,061
and broken commitments for years after

5
00:00:07,061 --> 00:00:08,810
they clearly stop working?

6
00:00:08,810 --> 00:00:11,999
Biologists Richard Dawkins and Tamsin Carlisle

7
00:00:11,999 --> 00:00:14,218
named it the Concorde Fallacy in

8
00:00:14,218 --> 00:00:14,564
1976,

9
00:00:14,564 --> 00:00:17,615
the year the supersonic jet entered service.

10
00:00:17,615 --> 00:00:20,388
Britain and France kept funding Concorde

11
00:00:20,388 --> 00:00:22,191
long after it was clear it

12
00:00:22,191 --> 00:00:24,340
would never pay back its costs.

13
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:26,633
Your brain hates admitting a loss

14
00:00:26,633 --> 00:00:29,134
so intensely that it throws precious

15
00:00:29,134 --> 00:00:32,191
future years after unrecoverable past years.

16
00:00:32,191 --> 00:00:34,137
Past time and past money are

17
00:00:34,137 --> 00:00:35,040
gone forever.

18
00:00:35,040 --> 00:00:38,202
Break the spell with the Zero-Base Question:

19
00:00:38,202 --> 00:00:40,502
knowing everything I know today,

20
00:00:40,502 --> 00:00:42,515
if I were not already inside

21
00:00:42,515 --> 00:00:45,174
this project or commitment right now,

22
00:00:45,174 --> 00:00:47,330
would I enter it from scratch?

23
00:00:47,330 --> 00:00:49,600
If the honest answer is no,

24
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:50,441
walk away.

25
00:00:50,441 --> 00:00:52,964
That frees your time and money

26
00:00:52,964 --> 00:00:54,730
for something better.
